<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mati'ilu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Also known as Mati'el</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mat-river">Mati</a>'ilu was the last independent king of Arpad, the Aramaean state of Bit-Agusi in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, in the mid-8th century BCE. He made a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashur-nirari-v">Ashur-nirari V</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and another, preserved on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sefire-steles">Sefire steles</a>, with Bar-Ga'yah of KTK. He later joined an alliance led by Urartu, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-iii">Tiglath-pileser III</a> besieged Arpad and annexed it in 740 BCE.</p></div>
